Layer 1: Foundation (What's actually happening underneath)
  → JPA vs Hibernate vs Spring Data JPA — the difference matters
  → EntityManager & Persistence Context
  → Entity Lifecycle States

Layer 2: Mapping (Beyond basic @Entity)
  → Relationships in depth — OneToMany, ManyToMany, cascade, fetch
  → Embeddables, Inheritance strategies
  → Composite Keys

Layer 3: Querying (Where most interviews go deep)
  → Derived query methods — how Spring generates SQL
  → JPQL vs Native Queries
  → @Query, @Modifying, @Transactional on queries
  → Criteria API (dynamic queries)
  → Projections & DTOs

Layer 4: Transactions (Critical for SDE2)
  → @Transactional internals — proxy mechanism
  → Propagation types — what each one means
  → Isolation levels — and real problems they solve
  → Common pitfalls (self-invocation, LazyInit exceptions)

Layer 5: Performance (What separates SDE2 from SDE1)
  → N+1 Problem — what it is, how to detect, how to fix
  → Fetch strategies — LAZY vs EAGER (and when each causes bugs)
  → Pagination & Sorting
  → First-level & Second-level Cache

Layer 6: Advanced (Bonus — makes you stand out)
  → Auditing (@CreatedDate, @LastModifiedBy)
  → Soft deletes
  → Custom Repository implementations
  → Spring Data Specifications
